<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS' GRUNDIG OUTSOURCES WORK TO ORIGIN.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS' GRUNDIG OUTSOURCES WORK TO ORIGIN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips' consumer products unit Grundig, based in Fuerth (Germany), will hand over part of its computer services to Origin, Grundig said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Origin will take over 110 of Grundig's employees throughout Europe.</p>
<p>Grundig said the move will be effective as of December 1 1996 and will further intensify the cooperation with Origin.</p>
<p>Grundig said it expected the move to increase productivity, to reduce costs and to raise efficiency.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
